    {
      "id": "MJUe",
      "code_hash": "678e75baf2ed9b028784bdf65b1f66b3",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"virtual-photons-and-qcd-radiation\">Virtual photons and QCD radiation</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><a href=\"/\">Browse notebooks</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"/?file=hep/soft_function.py\">Light-cone soft radiation</a> \u00b7\n<a href=\"/?file=hep/quark_gluon_scattering.py\">Quark\u2013gluon scattering</a></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Generate <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\gamma^*\\to\\mu^-\\mu^+||)</marimo-tex>, <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\gamma^*\\to q\\bar q||)</marimo-tex> and\nboth diagrams for <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\gamma^*\\to q\\bar qg||)</marimo-tex>. The massive squared\namplitudes are checked before taking the massless limit used for the\nDalitz distribution and regulated integral.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This covers FeynCalc's <a href=\"https://feyncalc.github.io/FeynCalcExamples/QED/Tree/Ga-MuAmu\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">muon-pair</a>,\n<a href=\"https://feyncalc.github.io/FeynCalcExamples/QCD/Tree/Ga-QQbar\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">quark-pair</a>, and\n<a href=\"https://feyncalc.github.io/FeynCalcExamples/QCD/Tree/Ga-QQbarGl\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">real-radiation</a>\nexamples. All particles are selected by name.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The virtual-photon current is contracted with <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(-g_{\\mu\\nu}||)</marimo-tex> without\nan initial spin average, matching those references. Its invariant mass is\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(Q=\\sqrt{q^2}&gt;0||)</marimo-tex>. These are timelike current rates, not decays of an\non-shell photon.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
